{"agent":"fix-bp","data":{"by":"fix-bp","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":1,"detail":"A valid fixed-mode configuration `parallel=fixed`, `max_parallel_tasks=1` with the default `max_parallel_min=2` now produces `FC.Params(start=1, floor=2, ceiling=1)`. `max_parallel_tasks` is allowed to be 1 by its `int_at_least(1)` check, and the change makes fixed mode use `max_parallel_min` as the floor without ensuring `max_parallel_min <= max_parallel_tasks` in fixed mode (the schedule doc still says this constraint is only “in auto”). A floor above the ceiling is an impossible interval for the adaptive governor and violates the intent that fixed mode never exceed `max_parallel_tasks`; either the config must be rejected, the floor clamped to `min(max_parallel_min, max_parallel_tasks)`, or the default/constraint must require `max_parallel_min <= max_parallel_tasks` in fixed mode too.","digest":"9f28d00074f6c34a","location":"ddflow/core/flowparams.py:floor=s.max_parallel_min","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/core/flowparams.py:floor=s.max_parallel_min"}],"diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"output_digest":"c4e74eb281c763d5","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/fix-Bd07c080a0c.rubber_duck.lan-deepseek-v4-pro.20261104T194622Z-a3323d49.jsonl","review_kind":"delta","reviewed":[1],"status":"PARTIAL","terminated_by":"SIGTERM","tree_sha":"102e8fdb7712+clean"},"gate":"rubber_duck","reason":"the review was terminated by SIGTERM mid-round after 1 chunk(s) were reviewed (1); those findings are checkpointed, the remaining chunks were not reviewed, which is not a pass"},"id":"e308c033ed80143a00e850a8d","kind":"gate.partial","lamport":136431,"schema":1,"subject":"fix-Bd07c080a0c","ts":"2026-11-04T19:48:06.104032Z"}
