{"agent":"fix-bp","data":{"by":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Pro-0813-Godzila","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":1,"detail":"In fixed mode `floor` is now taken from `s.max_parallel_min` unconditionally, but there is no corresponding validation that `max_parallel_min <= max_parallel_tasks` in fixed mode; the schedule config still documents that constraint only for `auto`. Given `[schedule] parallel = \"fixed\"`, `max_parallel_tasks = 1`, and default `max_parallel_min = 2` (both pass their per-knob `int_at_least(1)` checks), `params()` returns `Params(start=1, floor=2, ceiling=1)`. That makes the floor exceed the fixed ceiling, violating the new invariant that `max_parallel_tasks` is the ceiling and `max_parallel_min` is the floor. Before this change the same config produced `floor=1, ceiling=1`, so this is a regression for fixed mode with `max_parallel_tasks` below the default/configured minimum.","digest":"211f0f99b8c84f73","location":"ddflow/core/flowparams.py:params","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/core/flowparams.py:params"}],"chunks_total":5,"coverage":"5/5 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":1,"diff_chars":18820,"diff_sha":"d45e1f1070520cfab6a6a570e530452c24acaf8412e698992af02a4614ff1d3e","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in [REDACTED:path]","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":483.5,"excluded_bytes":2273,"excluded_files":1,"excluded_paths":["README.md"],"family":"deepseek","findings":1,"max_chunk_chars":5000,"model":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Pro-0813-Godzila","output_digest":"d90dfa508d6a8823","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/fix-Bd07c080a0c.rubber_duck.lan-deepseek-v4-pro.20261104T194839Z-6e859728.jsonl","reason":"","review_kind":"full","reviewed":[1,2,3,4,5],"reviewed_head":"102e8fdb77125ed83917ad6f761ba923c8cd64c9","reviewed_paths":{"README.md":"100644 e891490635a972a7dc7c3c66661a3488731554e3","ddflow/config_sections/schedule.py":"100644 373e559325bd41bf06fbe8f94f0b53aa327f3fb4","ddflow/c