{"agent":"fix-bp","data":{"by":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Pro-0813-Godzila","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":1,"detail":"`parallel=fixed` now returns `floor=s.max_parallel_min` while `ceiling=s.max_parallel_tasks`, but `max_parallel_min` is only checked with `int_at_least(1)` and the docs still only require it not to exceed `max_parallel_tasks` in `auto`. A valid configuration such as `parallel=fixed` with `max_parallel_tasks=1` and the default `max_parallel_min=2` therefore produces `Params(floor=2, ceiling=1, start=1)`, an impossible range that violates the fixed-mode contract “never exceeding the fixed number.” The change should have made `max_parallel_min <= max_parallel_tasks` mandatory in fixed mode (or clamped the floor), but does neither.","digest":"bf6154436eeba2c9","location":"ddflow/core/flowparams.py:floor=s.max_parallel_min","severity":"HIGH","title":"ddflow/core/flowparams.py:floor=s.max_parallel_min"},{"chunk":2,"detail":"The new fixed-mode branch calls `_words(parallel.limited_by)` whenever `limit < cfg.schedule.max_parallel_tasks`, but it does not first guard `parallel.limited_by == LIMIT_UNAVAILABLE` the way the existing auto branch in this same function does. In a normal fixed run with no limiting signal and fewer independent ready tasks than `max_parallel_tasks`, `limit` is below max while `parallel.limited_by` is `LIMIT_UNAVAILABLE`; `_words` has no mapping for that sentinel and raises `KeyError` while formatting `status`/`brief`. Example: fixed `max_parallel_tasks=8`, only 3 independent tasks available, no load/memory/disk/latency/gate signal.","digest":"9de1d377881d8f63","location":"ddflow/core/schedule/_parallel.py:_parallel_line","severity":"HIGH","title":"ddflow/core/schedule/_parallel.py:_parallel_line"},{"chunk":4,"detail":"`SPIKED` feeds the fake source under the key `\"load\"`, but the controller signal used by this same test file is `\"load_per_core\"` (`FC.Sample(..., {\"load_per_core\": 2.0})` and the assertion `d.limited_by == \"load_per_core\"`). `SIG.FakeSource` returns the keys it is given; it does not translate `\"load\"` into `\"load_per_core\"`. With no `load_per_core` sample ever recorded, `current_limit` cannot lower the fixed ceiling from 16, so `d.limit < cfg.schedule.max_parallel_tasks` and `d.limited_by == \"load_per_core\"` fail.","digest":"794ed72ab611f159","location":"tests/test_fixed_governor.py:24","severity":"HIGH","title":"tests/test_fixed_governor.py:24"}],"chunks_total":5,"coverage":"5/5 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":18820,"diff_sha":"d45e1f1070520cfab6a6a570e530452c24acaf8412e698992af02a4614ff1d3e","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in [REDACTED:path]","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":366.0,"excluded_bytes":2273,"excluded_files":1,"excluded_paths":["README.md"],"family":"deepseek","findings":3,"max_chunk_chars":5000,"model":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Pro-0813-Godzila","output_digest":"145284df13d832f4","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/fix-Bd07c080a0c.critic.lan-deepseek-v4-pro.20261104T195939Z-453b0349.jsonl","reason":"","review_kind":"full","reviewed":[1,2,3,4,5],"reviewed_head":"102e8fdb77125ed83917ad6f761ba923c8cd64c9","reviewed_paths":{"README.md":"100644 e891490635a972a7dc7c3c66661a3488731554e3","ddflow/config_sections/schedule.py":"100644 373e559325bd41bf06fbe8f94f0b53aa327f3fb4","ddflow/core/flowparams.py":"100644 0984fa467427a1c1c4a87ed8beff6bf129d2cfbb","ddflow/core/schedule/_parallel.py":"100644 ff94ba2b17ec8f7101184ea28f03c2c464b9ba23","ddflow/services/flowstate.py":"100644 9339f2dc97a1da3a7ead15c41d812d78010aa026","ddflow/services/ticks.py":"100644 a64a24d56aa9e7c4bb251a67bc2120362df8da8a","tests/test_adaptive_config.py":"100644 cb6c914768a01d37f9e800a02fffd9596ea46774","tests/test_doctor_flow_history.py":"100644 df4c617cc940edf66b463299aa6914b18a2de569","tests/test_fixed_governor.py":"100644 9ce0274001e0b9d65210cb3bfcc7edd98d589b33","tests/test_flowstate.py":"100644 3